  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1 ast-no-date-box\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n\n<p><!-- .entry-header --></p>\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Information :</strong> <span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><a style=\"color: #ff0000;\" href=\"https://www.sarkariexam.com/bpsc-school-teacher-tre-4-0-2026/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bihar Public Service Commission (BPSC)</a></span> has released the notification for the TRE 4.0 recruitment of School Teacher posts on the official website of BPSC. As per the notification, the online application process for Bihar School Teacher TRE 4.0 Recruitment 2026 will start soon. Tentatively, there are a total of 32,388 vacancies that have been issued in the Bihar School Teacher TRE 4.0 Recruitment 2026 for Middle School Teachers, Secondary Teachers, and Higher Secondary Teacher posts. Candidates must check the tentative details for Bihar School Teacher TRE 4.0 Recruitment 2026 given below.</span></span></span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 1.34953%;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Bihar Public Service Commission (BPSC)</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">BPSC School Teacher TRE 4.0 Recruitment 2026</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" style=\"width: 1.34953%;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Application Start Date : <strong>21 September 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Last Date : </span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><b>Notify Soon</b></span></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Fee Payment Last Date : <strong>Notify Soon</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Exam Date : <strong>Notify Soon</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Admit Card : <strong>Before Exam</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Result Available : <strong>Before Exam</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" style=\"width: 1.34953%;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">All Candidates : <strong>Rs. 100/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Bank Charge :&nbsp;<strong>Extra</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates have to pay their Examination Fee Through Debit Card / Credit Card / Net Banking / UPI and Other Fee Payment Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">[adinserter block=”3″]</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" style=\"width: 1.34953%;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>BPSC School Teacher TRE 4.0 Notification 2026 : Age Limit</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Age Limit As On 01 August 2025</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Minimum Age :&nbsp;<strong>18 Years (Class 1, to 05 &amp; 6 to 8)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Minimum Age :&nbsp;<strong>21 Years (Class 9 to 10 &amp; 11 to 12)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>37 Years (General Male)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>40 Years (General Female)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>40 Years (BC, EBC Male &amp; Female)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>42 Years (SC, ST Male &amp; Female)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Age Relaxation as per BPSC School Teacher TRE 4.0 Recruitment Rules.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\"> </span>Tool – </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" style=\"width: 1.34953%;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>BPSC School Teacher TRE 4.0 2026 : Vacancy Details</strong></span></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Total Posts : 32,388 Posts</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>No. of Posts</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Primary School Teacher (Class 1-5)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">3887</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Middle School Teacher (Class 6-8)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">8563</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">TGT Secondary School Teacher (Class 9-10)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">3877</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">TGT Secondary School Teacher (Class 9-10 Special)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">—</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">PGT Secondary School Teacher (Class 11-12)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">16101</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" style=\"width: 1.34953%;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>BPSC School Teacher TRE 4.0 Online Form 2026 : Educational Qualification&nbsp;</b></span></h3>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Eligibility&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Primary School Teacher (Class 1-5)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Graduation Degree in Any Stream with Diploma in Elementary Education<strong> OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Graduation Degree with 50% Marks and B.Ed Degree <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">12th with 50% Marks with 2 Year Diploma in Elementary Education / Special Diploma <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">12th with 45% Marks (As per 2002 Norms) with 2 Year Diploma in Elementary Education<strong> OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">12th with 50% Marks with 4 Year BLEd Degree <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Master Degree with 55% Marks and B.Ed – M.Ed 3 Year Degree.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">CTET Paper I <strong>OR</strong> BTET Paper I Exam Qualified.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Middle School Teacher (Class 6-8)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Graduation Degree with 50% Marks &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Graduation / Post Graduation Degree with 50% Marks with B.Ed&nbsp; <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Graduation Degree with 45% Marks and B.Ed (NCTE Norms) <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Graduation Degree with 50% Marks and BA BED and B.Sc Ed <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Graduation Degree with 50% Marks and B.Ed Special <strong>OR</strong>&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Post Graduation Degree with 55% Marks and 3 Year B.Ed – M.Ed Course. <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Graduation Degree in Any Stream with Diploma in Elementary Education</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">CTET Paper II Qualified</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">School Teacher (Class 6-8)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Graduation /&nbsp;Post Graduation Degree in Related Subject with Minimum 50% Marks &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong style=\"font-family: inherit;\">OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Graduation /&nbsp;Post Graduation in Related Subject with Minimum 45% Marks (As per 2002 Norms) &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong style=\"font-family: inherit;\">OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">4 Year Degree in BAEd/ BScEd</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">STET Paper I Exam Qualified</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">TGT Secondary School Teacher (Class 9-10)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Graduation /&nbsp;Post Graduation Degree in Related Subject with Minimum 50% Marks &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong style=\"font-family: inherit;\">OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Graduation /&nbsp;Post Graduation in Related Subject with Minimum 45% Marks (As per 2002 Norms) &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong style=\"font-family: inherit;\">OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">4 Year Degree in BAEd/ BScEd</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">STET Paper I Exam Qualified</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">TGT Secondary School Teacher (Class 9-10 Special)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Graduation /&nbsp;Post Graduation Degree in Related Subject with Minimum 50% Marks &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong style=\"font-family: inherit;\">OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Graduation /&nbsp;Post Graduation in Related Subject with Minimum 45% Marks (As per 2002 Norms) &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong style=\"font-family: inherit;\">OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">4 Year Degree in BAEd/ BScEd</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">STET Paper I Exam Qualified</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 31.9918%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">PGT Secondary School Teacher (Class 11-12)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 68.0082%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Master Degree in Related Subject with Minimum 50% Marks &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Master Degree in Related Subject with Minimum 45% Marks (As per 2002 Norms) &amp; B.Ed Degree <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Master Degree in Related Subject with 4 Year Degree in BAEd / BScEd <strong>OR</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Master Degree with 55% Marks &amp; B.Ed – M.Ed 3 Year Degree.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">STET Paper II Exam Qualified.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" style=\"width: 1.34953%;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>BPSC School Teacher TRE 4.0 Online Form 2026 : How To Apply</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates can apply through link https://bpsc.bihar.gov.in/ or provided below in link section or they can also apply through official site of the BPSC before Last Date.</span></li